[h2][b]Installation[/b][/h2]

You can download the latest version via Steam client - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=]Station Auto Builder[/url]
Or you can do it via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/]Station Auto Builder[/url]

[h2][b]Save state[/b][/h2]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[h2][b]Usage[/b][/h2]

Open the build menu of one of your stations. The planner panel sits under the menu's title bar.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationAutoBuilder/refs/heads/main/docs/images/panel_bill.png[/img]
[list=1]
[*] Pick a category and a module from your blueprints, set the count, press Add. Repeat for every module type you want; a row's X removes it, Clear empties the bill.
[*] Press Run. Modules are placed one after another; the panel counts placed, failed and left. Stop halts the run after the current module.
[*] When the run ends, check the plan, move or remove what you like by hand, and press Apply as usual. The build menu's own Cancel discards the whole unconfirmed plan. Optimize plot fits the plot to the planned modules on every side (the smallest plot on an empty plan), so a plot a run grew or one you emptied is not paid larger than needed.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationAutoBuilder/refs/heads/main/docs/images/panel_running.png[/img]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-StationAutoBuilder/refs/heads/main/docs/images/build_menu_run.png[/img]

Connection modules in the bill are not placed as such: they are the budget of connectors the planner may insert when a module finds no free connection. Big modules go first and nearest to the station's centre, docks, piers, build and defence modules on outward connections with clearance around them.

[h2][b]Options[/b][/h2]

In the game's Extension Options, the Station Auto Builder page has a Debug Level setting (None, Debug, Trace) for the game log.

